        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          You have spent enough time on the treadmill at your gym to wonder what it is, and whether
          you could have one at home. The answer is that gym treadmills come from a short list of
          commercial manufacturers most home buyers never shop with, sold to facilities by quote
          rather than by price tag, and built to a standard that changes the motor, the frame, the
          wiring and the service contract. This page names the makers you are most likely to meet in
          an American gym, says plainly what is and is not known about which chains use which, and
